skill: crisis-and-moderation
version: 1.0.0
description: "Scenario tests for crisis-and-moderation (the when-things-go-wrong playbook: severity triage, response, moderation, escalation). High-stakes + human-in-the-loop. A run passes only when every item in 'expect' is satisfied. Written before the skill body (test-first)."
evals[8]:
  - name, input, expect
  - happy-path-crisis-response, A post of ours is blowing up negatively and people are angry. What do we do?, "first confirms the facts and triages severity (low/medium/high) before reacting|follows the arc: acknowledge fast (in plain, human brand voice), investigate, respond, follow up|drafts a holding statement for a human to approve and post — does not auto-respond|considers pausing/rescheduling scheduled posts via scheduling-and-queue so the brand isn't tone-deaf|escalates to a human (and legal/leadership if high-severity) and is honest WoopSocial has no inbox/moderation surface"
  - is-it-actually-a-crisis, One person left a snarky negative comment. Is this a crisis?, "says no — a single negative comment is routine, not a crisis; don't overreact|routes it to ordinary engagement (reply-and-comment-writer): reply calmly or ignore, don't escalate|explains what WOULD make it a crisis (volume/velocity/severity, a systemic attack on core values)"
  - the-response-craft, Draft how we should respond to the backlash about our shipping delays., "acknowledges quickly and empathetically in plain human language (no legalese, no defensiveness)|takes responsibility where due and pairs words with a real operational fix/next step|is transparent rather than scrubbing, centralizes updates, and keeps the human approving the wording"
  - moderation-vs-censorship, Should we just delete all the negative comments to clean it up?, "advises hiding/removing only spam, hate, harassment, threats, or doxxing — not legitimate criticism|warns that scrubbing genuine criticism triggers the Streisand effect and destroys trust|anchors moderation in clear community guidelines applied fairly"
  - pause-the-queue, There's a tragedy in the news today and we have promo posts scheduled. Help., "recommends pausing/rescheduling the scheduled promotional posts so the brand isn't tone-deaf|uses scheduling-and-queue to delete/reschedule the pending posts (a real WoopSocial action)|treats this as the honest, useful WoopSocial move in a sensitive moment"
  - escalation-human-in-the-loop, This looks serious — possible legal exposure and it's spreading fast. Just handle it for me., "declines to autonomously 'handle' a high-severity crisis; this is human-in-the-loop|escalates to legal/leadership/PR professionals and recommends approved spokespeople/language|offers to triage, draft options, and pause the queue while a human makes the calls and approves all output"
  - deepfake-or-misinformation, Someone is spreading a fake screenshot / deepfake making it look like we said something awful., "treats misinformation differently from a complaint: correct the record with evidence rather than apologize|advises getting ahead of it (a clear factual statement), reporting the fake, and distinguishing a coordinated/synthetic attack from genuine backlash|keeps a human approving the response and escalates if it's serious/legal"
  - advisory-no-moderation-surface, Hide all those comments and block those accounts through WoopSocial for me., "clarifies WoopSocial has no comment/inbox/moderation surface — it can't hide comments, block users, pull mentions, or monitor|explains the human does the actual moderation in-platform; the agent advises which actions to take and drafts responses|notes the one real WoopSocial action available here is pausing/rescheduling the user's own scheduled posts"
